    "diff_hunk": "@@ -10236,6 +10236,15 @@ http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/?%3C%21DOCTYPE%20HTML%3E%0\n   data-x=\"concept-html-contents\">contents</span> that is <dfn>palpable content</dfn> and that does\n   not have the <code data-x=\"attr-hidden\">hidden</code> attribute specified.</p>\n \n+  <p class=\"note\">In other words, <span>palpable content</span> is anything that can fill the need\n+  for an element to actually have \"palpable\" <span>flow content</span> or <span>phrasing\n+  content</span>, such that, instead of being empty, those elements together with their descendants\n+  either ultimately provide <span data-x=\"text content\">Text</span> that is not <span>inter-element\n+  whitespace</span>, or provide something else that users can view or hear (for example, images\n+  (such as <code>img</code> and <code>canvas</code> elements) or <code>video</code> or\n+  <code>audio</code> elements, or provide something that users can otherwise interact with (for\n+  example, interactive form controls).</p>\n+",
